# No license key. CFF 1.2.0 constrains it to an SPDX identifier, and this
# repository has no single one: the upstream code is MIT, (c) 2024 Elena
# Natterer, while the thesis text, figures, checkpoints and result artifacts
# added here are not covered by that grant. "Proprietary" was not an SPDX
# identifier, so the file failed schema validation and GitHub would not render
# the citation widget; "MIT" would validate by misstating the terms of the
# added material. The split is stated exactly in LICENSE and in the "Licence
# and attribution" section of README.md.
